{
  "name": "FluxFilm · 04 Uptime + deploy watch",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🩺 FluxFilm uptime + deploy watch — SETUP\n**(a) Uptime** — every 5 minutes it calls `/n8n/api/health`. If the answer is not 200, takes over **5 s**, or the **database is down**, you get ONE alert. No more alerts until it is back; then a ✅ recovery message.\n**(b) Deploy watch** — when you push to `oliviaharsh/fluxfilm-cache-server` **main** (= merge a PR), it waits 4 min, then compares the sha256 of `server.js` + `index.html` at that commit with the fingerprint the live shop reports. Still different after 3 checks (12 min) → alert “Hostinger did not deploy — press Redeploy in hPanel”.\n\n1. Credentials: `FluxFilm n8n key` (Header Auth), `GitHub FluxFilm` (GitHub API, a token with repo read + webhook admin), `SMTP FluxFilm (Gmail app password)`. Optional: `Telegram FluxFilm bot`, `Pushover (optional)` then enable those nodes.\n2. Put your email in both **Email** nodes.\n3. GitHub webhook not possible (no admin rights / private network)? Disable **GitHub push to main** and enable the 3 nodes of **Poll GitHub every 10 min**.\n4. **Active** on. (The “already alerted” memory only works in active runs, not in manual test runs.)\nApp folder inside the repo is `fluxfilm-cache-server/` — change APP_DIR in **Commit info** if you move it.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "4e828999-3111-48a8-a649-cceafe96439f",
